--- a/DEPLOY.md
+++ b/DEPLOY.md
@@ -53,12 +53,21 @@ This creates the category tree, the admin user, sample products and 2 coupons. O
 - Cloudinary: copy the three values. Uploads land in the `shyfly/` folder.
 - Resend: verify the sending domain (DNS records), then set `EMAIL_FROM="Shyfly <orders@yourdomain.in>"`. Without email, password-reset links print in the server log, and order emails are skipped.
 
+## 7b. Invoice delivery (email + WhatsApp)
+- Every confirmed order generates a PDF invoice (`backend/utils/invoicePdf.js`, fonts in `backend/assets/`). Customers get it by email as an attachment; the admin has one-click **WhatsApp invoice / update** buttons (wa.me links, free).
+- **Email provider (pick one):**
+  - **Brevo** (free tier, no domain): create account → Senders → add + verify the shop's email address → SMTP & API → create an API key → set `BREVO_API_KEY` and `EMAIL_FROM="Shyfly <that-verified-address>"`. (Free-mail senders such as Gmail can land in spam; a domain email is better when available.)
+  - **Resend**: needs a verified domain to send to customers → `RESEND_API_KEY`, `EMAIL_FROM="Shyfly <orders@yourdomain.in>"`.
+  - Render's free plan blocks classic SMTP ports, so use these HTTP APIs (already how the code works).
+- `PUBLIC_API_URL` is optional on Render (it provides `RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL`); set it if you use a custom API domain, otherwise invoice links in emails/WhatsApp point to the wrong host.
+- **Optional automatic WhatsApp** (Meta WhatsApp Cloud API): create a Meta Business app + WhatsApp number, create an approved *utility* template with 4 body variables — e.g. `Hi {{1}}, thank you for your Shyfly order {{2}} (₹{{3}}). Download your invoice: {{4}}` — then set `WHATSAPP_TOKEN`, `WHATSAPP_PHONE_ID`, `WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE` (+ `WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANG`). Meta charges per business-initiated message and needs business verification; this path is untested here, so test it with your own number first.
+
 ## 8. Go-live test (do all of these on production)
 - [ ] COD order → appears in Admin → Orders; stock decreases
 - [ ] Online order (live ₹1 product) → "paid" automatically; webhook shows delivered in Razorpay dashboard
 - [ ] Admin → Refund works; Cancel restocks
 - [ ] Mark an order Delivered → customer requests a return → approve → received → refund (online order) works
-- [ ] Invoice prints with business name/GSTIN (fill Store settings first)
+- [ ] Invoice PDF downloads (Track Order) with business name/GSTIN (fill Store settings first); order email arrives with the PDF attached; Admin → Order → WhatsApp invoice opens WhatsApp with the right number
 - [ ] Pincode check on product page; a blocked pincode is rejected at checkout
 - [ ] Forgot-password email arrives and works
 - [ ] Mobile: browse, bag, checkout
diff --git a/HANDOVER.md b/HANDOVER.md
index 3a3d268..ea938ee 100644
--- a/HANDOVER.md
+++ b/HANDOVER.md
@@ -23,6 +23,15 @@ Orders → click an order → set **Status** as you go: Confirmed → Packed →
 - **Refund an online payment:** open the order → **Refund via Razorpay**. Money goes back to the customer's original method (usually 5–7 working days).
 - **Invoice:** **Print invoice** button (print or save as PDF).
 
+### Sending the invoice to a customer
+- **Email (automatic):** if email is set up, every order email goes out with the **invoice PDF attached** to the customer's email address (they type it at checkout). Check Store settings → Setup checklist to see if email is on.
+- **WhatsApp (free, one click):** open the order → **WhatsApp invoice**. WhatsApp opens with the customer's number and a ready message containing the invoice PDF link — just press send. **WhatsApp update** does the same for status/tracking updates.
+- **Email again:** open the order → **Email invoice** (only shows if the customer gave an email).
+- The customer can also download the PDF anytime from Track Order or My account.
+
+### Deleting many products at once
+Products → tick the boxes (the top box ticks the whole page) → **Delete**, **Hide** or **Show** in the bar that appears. After ticking a full page, click **Select all N matching** to act on every product in the current search. Past orders keep their product details. Deleting cannot be undone — use **Hide** if unsure.
+
 ### Returns & exchanges
 Customers request these themselves from **Track Order** (or My account) once an order is **Delivered**, within your return window (Store settings → Return window; set 0 to turn returns off). You see them under **Returns** (and a banner on the Dashboard).
 1. **Approve** or **Reject** (write a message — the customer sees it on Track Order).
diff --git a/backend/.env.example b/backend/.env.example
index 63572b6..3722598 100644
--- a/backend/.env.example
+++ b/backend/.env.example
@@ -31,9 +31,23 @@ CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
 CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
 CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
 
-# Email via Resend (optional)
+# Public URL of this API — used in invoice links. Render sets RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL automatically;
+# set this only if you use a custom API domain (e.g. https://api.yourdomain.in)
+PUBLIC_API_URL=
+
+# Email (invoice PDF is attached to the order email). Use ONE provider:
+#  - Brevo: free tier, NO domain needed — verify a sender address (e.g. your Gmail) in Brevo, then set EMAIL_FROM to it
+#  - Resend: free tier, but you must verify your own domain before it can email customers
+BREVO_API_KEY=
 RESEND_API_KEY=
 ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL=
 
+# OPTIONAL automatic WhatsApp invoice (Meta WhatsApp Cloud API — Meta charges a small per-message fee).
+# Without it, use the one-click "WhatsApp invoice" button on each order in the admin (free).
+WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
+WHATSAPP_PHONE_ID=
+WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE=
+WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANG=en
+
 # Sender shown on emails. Must be on a domain verified in Resend, e.g. Shyfly <orders@shyfly.in>
 EMAIL_FROM=
